{{!-- A Scar, told to the table in one card. The caption is the message's `flavor` ("Scars").

      It starts as a notice — who owes a Scar and how much the hit took — with the button that
      opens the Scars window, the way back in for a player who closed it or was away when the hit
      landed. When the window rolls, it rewrites this card line by line as each die lands, and the
      button goes, because the Scar is taken. A notice the Warden posted for an absent player is
      not the player's to rewrite: it keeps its button, and the button refuses once the Scar is
      taken (module/cairn2e.js). A gain rolled later from the Growth tab posts the
      same card with its own lines and no HP figure. --}}
{{#if notice}}
<p>{{localize 'CAIRN.Scar.Notice' name=name lost=lost}}</p>
<button type="button" class="cairn-card-action open-scars"><i class="fa-solid fa-heart-crack" inert></i> {{localize 'CAIRN.Scar.Open'}}</button>
{{else}}
<p class="cairn-card-lead">{{name}}</p>
{{#if lost}}
<p class="cairn-card-note">{{localize 'CAIRN.Scar.LostNote' lost=lost}}</p>
{{/if}}
{{#if lines.length}}
<ul class="cairn-damage-state cairn-scar-lines">
    {{#each lines as |l|}}
    <li class="{{l.tone}}">
        <span class="cairn-damage-label">{{l.label}}</span>
        <span class="cairn-damage-value">{{l.value}}</span>
    </li>
    {{/each}}
</ul>
{{/if}}
{{#if rolling}}
<p class="cairn-card-note">{{localize 'CAIRN.Scar.Rolling'}}</p>
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
